Subject: [PATCH] riscv: fix single-hart initialization without the hart lottery

Upstream-Status: Pending

A single-hart image does not need the atomic hart lottery. Skip it when
SMP is disabled, so single-hart CPUs can initialize without requiring
atomic instructions for boot-hart selection.

The common initialization path also uses s2 as the lottery result.
Initialize it to zero when bypassing the lottery, including XIP builds,
so the boot hart follows the initialization path deterministically.
Keep the existing handling of unexpected non-boot harts.

diff --git a/arch/riscv/cpu/start.S b/arch/riscv/cpu/start.S
--- a/arch/riscv/cpu/start.S
+++ b/arch/riscv/cpu/start.S
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@ call_board_init_f_0:
 call_harts_early_init:
 	jal	harts_early_init
 
-#if !CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(XIP)
+#if !CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(XIP) && CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SMP)
 	/*
 	 * Pick hart to initialize global data and run U-Boot. The other harts
 	 * wait for initialization to complete.
@@ -155,12 +155,12 @@ call_harts_early_init:
 	bnez	s2, wait_for_gd_init
 #else
 	/*
-	 * FIXME: gp is set before it is initialized. If an XIP U-Boot ever
-	 * encounters a pending IPI on boot it is liable to jump to whatever
-	 * memory happens to be in ipi_data.addr on boot. It may also run into
-	 * problems if it encounters an exception too early (because printf/puts
-	 * accesses gd).
+	 * A single-hart image has no lottery to run, and an XIP image cannot
+	 * mutate lock variables in flash. Park any unexpected non-boot hart.
+	 * Keep the lottery result zero so the common path below takes the boot
+	 * hart branch.
 	 */
+	li	s2, 0
 	mv	gp, s0
 #if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(RISCV_MMODE)
 	bnez	tp, secondary_hart_loop
